      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "1. Index: \r\nActive component \r\n- This is a component that relies on
    an external trigger source to control, activate or perform its task.\r\n\r\nCalibration
    \r\n-\tIt is the process of determining, rectifying, and marking the readings
    of an instrument with those of a standard device in order to check the instruments
    accuracy. \r\n\r\nInternet Protocol \r\n-\tIt is a set of guidelines that direct
    the format of data sent over the internet or another network.\r\n\r\nProjector:
    \r\n-\tA device that is used to emit rays of light that will display as a screen
    on the hitting surface, it is a device with a system of lenses for projecting
    slides or films on to a screen. In this document, mostly called the projected
    screen.  \r\n\r\nProjector \r\n-\tA device that is used to emit rays of light
    that will display as a screen on the hitting surface, it is a device with a system
    of lenses for projecting slides or films on to a screen. In this document, mostly
    called the projected screen.\r\n\r\nPassive component \r\n-\tThis is a component
    that does not requires an external trigger or signal to activate its functions.
    As the system is running, the component is continuously active.\r\n\r\nScene:
    \r\n-\tIn unity, a scene is a visual environment built with unity tools. Think
    of a scene as a different level in a game, or different scenario in a movie.
    In this project, every required scenario is built is a scene \r\n \r\nScreen
    frame resolution: \r\n-\tThe number of pixels a monitor or projected screen can
    show horizontally and vertically. \r\n\r\nSimulator \r\n-\tA simulator is a system
    that mimics the operation of an existing or proposed system, providing the ability
    to test different scenarios or process changes.\r\n\r\nScene \r\n-\tIn unity,
    a scene is a visual environment built with unity tools. Think of a scene in unity
    as a different levels, in this project every required scenario is built in a
    scene.\r\n\r\nUDP \u2013 User Datagram Protocol \r\n-\tThe user datagram protocol
    is a communication method that uses the internet protocol to transfer data from
    one device to another, or one software to another. \r\n-\tInternet Protocol (IP),
    is the set of rules conducting the format of data sent through the internet or
    other networks. \r\nACC \u2013 Accurate Coordinate Calculation\r\n-\tThe ACC
    calculation is an embedded function in the system used to enhance the accuracy
    of the hit points in the system when shooting.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n2.\tSoftware application 
    \r\nThe software consists of five categories, namely; Login, Calibration, Main
    Menu, Training Settings, and Scenario. \r\n\r\na.\tLOGIN: login page is the access
    point of the system. In order to have access to the software you are required
    to enter your designated Imagistix email address and password.\r\nb.\tCALIBRATION:
    The calibration scene is fully autonomous, it is the highest requirement for
    the system to function fully. On this stage, you should ensure that the camera
    is pointed directly at the projected screen, note that the optimal position for
    the camera is the center of the screen. If not possible, then the ACC procedure
    will be required. Do not disturb calibration until it is complete.\r\nc.\tMAIN
    MENU: This is the control center of the system. On this scene you get access
    to all system settings, list of scenarios and control buttons.\r\nd.\tTRAINING
    SETTINGS: This page allows you to set and control all the requirements of the
    selected training scenario. You can set the total time, number of targets, number
    of magazines, and total ammunition required to be used in the training.\r\ne.\tSCENARIO:
    This is the running visual representation of the scene you selected in the main
    menu. It is what the trainee will interact with during training.\r\n\r\n\r\n3.\tSoftware
    inventory\r\nThe system has a web-based intergraded scoring system called the
    OMP. The OMP gives access to the results of every training and allows you to
    keep track of the ranking. The ranking shows you the list of the top 5 shooters
    in all your recent trainees. Note, scoring does not always require you to keep
    your computer connected to the internet. You can run all your trainings offline,
    and connect once to the internet for the software to automatically upload the
    results to the OMP. Alternatively, you can keep your computer connected to the
    internet, and allow the software to automatically or manually save after every
    complete training.\r\n \r\n4.\tContingencies and alternate states and modes of
    operation\r\nIf in any case the camera does not pick up the shooting signal,
    or the system has stopped responding, follow the guidelines bellow on how to
    fix the issue:\r\na.\tOpen the VNC software installed in your computer, and click
    on the camera option. The software should open a window that allows you to have
    access to the camera microcontroller, in that window you have to see a visual
    display of your projector screen that is picked up by the connected camera. If
    you see the visual display but it does not show the current projector screen,
    you should unplug the microcontroller, and plug it back again to restart. If
    you see a visual display that the camera picks up, but it does not point to the
    projector screen, then gently adjust the camera to point directly to the projector
    screen, and go to the software to perform calibration again.\r\nb.\tIf the system
    is still not responding after following point \u201CA\u201D, please go to the
    IMX simulator software. In the main menu, you will find a logout button, please
    click on that button in order to restart the software without losing your system
    settings. Enter your login details again, and do not interrupt the system during
    calibration. \r\n\r\n5.\tAssistance and problem reporting\r\n If you encounter
    errors, glitches, or malfunctions in the software, or the hardware is not functioning
    during run time, please contact the company support service for help and maintenance
    \u2013 support@imagistix.co.za \r\n\r\n6.\tSecurity and privacy\r\nThe system
    is copyright reserved, you are not allowed to duplicate, sell, or rent to another
    party. If you are found against these terms, you will be prosecuted.\r\n\r\n7.\tQuick-Navigation
    guide \r\nBelow are the directories you need to know for all navigation functionalities
    available in the system, these are the keyboard commands you need: \r\nLeft Shift
    + Escape = Back to main menu \r\nLeft Shift + Plus = Increment the shot delay
    \r\nLeft Shift + Minus = Decrement the shoot delay \r\nLeft Shift + Back = Erase
    data on the indoor training score board \r\nLeft Shift + Space = Restart Scene
    \r\nLeft Shift + R = Reset paper shots and paper roll\r\nLeft Shift + F1 = register
    top left corner calibration point \r\nLeft Shift + F2 = register bottom right
    calibration point \r\nLeft Shift + F3 = calibration point\r\nUp button = Zoom
    In\r\nDown Button = Zoom Out\r\nLeft Button = Move left\r\nRight Button = Move
    right\r\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
