  m_text: "Active component \n- This is a component that relies on an external trigger
    source to control, activate or perform its task.\r\n\r\nCalibration \r\n- It
    is the process of determining, rectifying, and marking the readings of an instrument
    with those of a standard device in order to check the instruments accuracy. \r\n\r\nInternet
    Protocol \r\n- It is a set of guidelines that direct the format of data sent
    over the internet or another network.\r\n\r\nProjector: \r\n- A device that is
    used to emit rays of light that will display as a screen on the hitting surface,
    it is a device with a system of lenses for projecting slides or films on to a
    screen. In this document, mostly called the projected screen.  \r\n\r\nProjector
    \r\n- A device that is used to emit rays of light that will display as a screen
    on the hitting surface, it is a device with a system of lenses for projecting
    slides or films on to a screen. In this document, mostly called the projected
    screen.\r\n\r\nPassive component \r\n- This is a component that does not requires
    an external trigger or signal to activate its functions. As the system is running,
    the component is continuously active.\r\n\r\nScene: \r\n- In unity, a scene is
    a visual environment built with unity tools. Think of a scene as a different
    level in a game, or different scenario in a movie. In this project, every required
    scenario is built is a scene \r\n \r\nScreen frame resolution: \r\n- The number
    of pixels a monitor or projected screen can show horizontally and vertically.
    \r\n\r\nSimulator \r\n- A simulator is a system that mimics the operation of
    an existing or proposed system, providing the ability to test different scenarios
    or process changes.\r\n\r\nScene \r\n- In unity, a scene is a visual environment
    built with unity tools. Think of a scene in unity as a different levels, in this
    project every required scenario is built in a scene.\r\n\r\nUDP \u2013 User Datagram
    Protocol \r\n- The user datagram protocol is a communication method that uses
    the internet protocol to transfer data from one device to another, or one software
    to another. \r\n- Internet Protocol (IP), is the set of rules conducting the
    format of data sent through the internet or other networks. \r\n\nACC \u2013
    Accurate Coordinate Calculation\r\n- The ACC calculation is an embedded function
    in the system used to enhance the accuracy of the hit points in the system when
    shooting.\r"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
